            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0533" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-12T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>119. Your 168, September 6, noon.</p>
                <p>Following from Hill, American Red Cross: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your cables. Cannot determine course of action until Davis’ reports
                            received together with information as to International Relief <pb
                                facs="0534" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/> measures contemplated. From
                            meager reports available only action by government authorities could
                            adequately relieve situation. AmCross ready expend $25,000 as direct
                            contribution for temporary emergency work on the ground. For record
                            would prefer separate accounting direct to headquarters. Hill.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>You may draw on Department for $25,000 which has been deposited by Red Cross for
                    relief work as above indicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
